<title>USA: Lockheed jet fighter on Norway's short list.</title>
<headline>Lockheed jet fighter on Norway's short list.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Norway said Tuesday the Lockheed Martin Corp F-16C/D is one of two planes on its short list for a new fighter aircraft purchase.</p>
<p>Along with the F-16, Norway will also consider the Eurofighter 2000. Norway has eliminated the McDonnell Douglas Corp F/A-18 and Dassault Aviation's Rafale from consideration.</p>
<p>Norway's air force has flown versions of the F-16 since the 1980s and its existing F-16 fleet is being modernized as part of a five-nation update program that includes extensive participation by European industry.</p>
</text>
